"""Cybersecurity glossary, part 14: cryptography concepts, network basics, standards and privacy law, and the tools defenders use. Protective descriptions only.
fr/rw/sw are drafts for fluent review."""
from cyber_terms_12 import T

TERMS_14 = [
    T("plaintext-ciphertext", "Plaintext and ciphertext", ["plaintext", "ciphertext", "cipher", "cipher text", "encrypted text", "clear text"], "crypto", "encrypted message", {"fr": "Texte clair et texte chiffré", "sw": "Maandishi wazi na maandishi yaliyosimbwa", "rw": "Inyandiko isanzwe n'inyandiko ifunze"},
      ("Plaintext is readable information; ciphertext is the scrambled result after encryption. A cipher is the method (algorithm) that turns one into the other using a key.", "Only people with the right key can turn ciphertext back to plaintext. Never send passwords or PINs in plaintext (ordinary email, SMS) when a secure channel is available."),
      ("Le texte clair est une information lisible ; le texte chiffré est le résultat brouillé après chiffrement. Un chiffre (cipher) est la méthode (algorithme) qui transforme l'un en l'autre avec une clé.", "Seules les personnes ayant la bonne clé peuvent retrouver le texte clair. N'envoyez jamais mots de passe ou PIN en clair (e-mail, SMS ordinaires) quand un canal sécurisé existe."),
      ("Plaintext ni amakuru asomeka; ciphertext ni ibyavuye mu guhindurwa nyuma ya encryption. Cipher ni uburyo (algorithm) buhindura kimwe mu kindi bukoresheje urufunguzo.", "Abafite urufunguzo rukwiye gusa bashobora gusubiza ciphertext muri plaintext. Ntuzohereze amagambo y'ibanga cyangwa PIN mu nyandiko isanzwe (imeri, SMS bisanzwe) mu gihe hari inzira itekanye."),
      ("Plaintext ni taarifa inayosomeka; ciphertext ni matokeo yaliyochanganywa baada ya usimbaji. Cipher ni njia (algorithm) inayogeuza moja kuwa nyingine kwa ufunguo.", "Wenye ufunguo sahihi pekee wanaweza kurudisha ciphertext kuwa plaintext. Kamwe usitume nywila au PIN kama maandishi wazi (barua pepe, SMS za kawaida) wakati njia salama ipo.")),
    T("block-stream-cipher", "Block cipher and stream cipher", ["block cipher", "stream cipher", "cipher modes", "gcm mode", "cbc mode"], "crypto", "encryption blocks", {"fr": "Chiffrement par blocs et par flux", "sw": "Block cipher na stream cipher", "rw": "Block cipher na stream cipher"},
      ("A block cipher (such as AES) encrypts data in fixed-size blocks; a stream cipher (such as ChaCha20) encrypts it as a continuous stream. The “mode” (for example GCM) says how blocks are chained.", "Practical rule: use well-reviewed standard algorithms in safe modes (AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305) from trusted libraries. Never invent your own cipher or use old ones like DES and RC4."),
      ("Un chiffrement par blocs (comme AES) chiffre les données en blocs de taille fixe ; un chiffrement par flux (comme ChaCha20) les chiffre en flux continu. Le « mode » (par exemple GCM) décrit l'enchaînement des blocs.", "Règle pratique : utilisez des algorithmes standard bien examinés en modes sûrs (AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305) via des bibliothèques de confiance. N'inventez jamais votre chiffre et évitez les anciens comme DES et RC4."),
      ("Block cipher (nka AES) ifunga amakuru mu bice bingana buri gihe; stream cipher (nka ChaCha20) iyafunga nk'umugezi uhoraho. «Mode» (urugero GCM) ivuga uko ibice bihuzwa.", "Itegeko ry'ingenzi: koresha algorithms zisanzwe zasuzumwe neza mu buryo butekanye (AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305) uzikuye muri library zizewe. Ntuzahimbe cipher yawe cyangwa ngo ukoreshe izishaje nka DES na RC4."),
      ("Block cipher (kama AES) husimba data kwa vipande vya ukubwa sawa; stream cipher (kama ChaCha20) huisimba kama mkondo unaoendelea. «Mode» (mfano GCM) inasema vipande vinavyounganishwaje.", "Kanuni ya vitendo: tumia algorithms za kawaida zilizopitiwa vizuri kwa modi salama (AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305) kutoka maktaba zinazoaminika. Kamwe usibuni cipher yako wala kutumia za zamani kama DES na RC4.")),
    T("diffie-hellman", "Diffie-Hellman key exchange", ["diffie-hellman", "diffie hellman", "key exchange", "ecdh", "dh key exchange"], "crypto", "two people exchanging keys", {"fr": "Échange de clés Diffie-Hellman", "sw": "Ubadilishanaji wa funguo wa Diffie-Hellman", "rw": "Guhana imfunguzo kwa Diffie-Hellman"},
      ("A method that lets two parties agree on a shared secret key over an open network without ever sending the key itself, so eavesdroppers cannot work it out.", "It is used inside TLS, VPNs and messaging apps to start secure sessions (often as ECDH). “Ephemeral” versions give forward secrecy: a stolen long-term key cannot decrypt past conversations."),
      ("Méthode qui permet à deux parties de convenir d'une clé secrète partagée sur un réseau ouvert sans jamais envoyer la clé elle-même, de sorte qu'un espion ne peut pas la déduire.", "Utilisée dans TLS, les VPN et les messageries pour démarrer des sessions sécurisées (souvent en ECDH). Les versions « éphémères » donnent la confidentialité persistante : une clé à long terme volée ne déchiffre pas les conversations passées."),
      ("Uburyo bwemerera impande ebyiri kumvikana ku rufunguzo rw'ibanga rusangiwe kuri murandasi ifunguye nta kohereza urufunguzo ubwarwo, bityo uwumviriza adashobora kurubona.", "Bukoreshwa muri TLS, VPN na porogaramu z'ubutumwa mu gutangiza ibiganiro bitekanye (akenshi nka ECDH). Ubwoko bwa «ephemeral» butanga forward secrecy: urufunguzo rw'igihe kirekire rwibwe ntirushobora gufungura ibiganiro bya kera."),
      ("Njia inayoruhusu pande mbili kukubaliana ufunguo wa siri wa pamoja kwenye mtandao wazi bila kutuma ufunguo wenyewe, hivyo msikilizaji hawezi kuugundua.", "Hutumika ndani ya TLS, VPN na programu za ujumbe kuanzisha vikao salama (mara nyingi kama ECDH). Matoleo ya «ephemeral» hutoa forward secrecy: ufunguo wa muda mrefu ukiibwa hauwezi kufungua mazungumzo ya zamani.")),
    T("elliptic-curve-cryptography", "Elliptic-curve cryptography (ECC)", ["elliptic curve cryptography", "ecc", "ecdsa", "ed25519", "curve25519"], "crypto", "mathematical curve", {"fr": "Cryptographie sur courbes elliptiques", "sw": "Kriptografia ya mviringo wa elliptic", "rw": "Elliptic-curve cryptography"},
      ("A modern form of public-key cryptography based on the maths of elliptic curves that gives strong security with much shorter keys than RSA, so it is fast and light.", "Common in phones, TLS certificates, SSH keys and crypto-currencies (ECDSA, Ed25519). Choose well-known curves from trusted libraries; large quantum computers could one day break it, which is why post-quantum algorithms are being standardised."),
      ("Forme moderne de cryptographie à clé publique fondée sur les mathématiques des courbes elliptiques, offrant une sécurité forte avec des clés bien plus courtes que RSA, donc rapide et légère.", "Courante dans les téléphones, certificats TLS, clés SSH et cryptomonnaies (ECDSA, Ed25519). Choisissez des courbes connues via des bibliothèques de confiance ; de grands ordinateurs quantiques pourraient la casser un jour, d'où la standardisation d'algorithmes post-quantiques."),
      ("Uburyo bwa none bwa public-key cryptography bushingiye ku mibare ya elliptic curves butanga umutekano ukomeye ukoresheje imfunguzo ngufi cyane kurusha RSA, bityo ni bwihuse kandi bworoshye.", "Bukunze mu matelefone, certificates za TLS, imfunguzo za SSH na crypto-monnaies (ECDSA, Ed25519). Hitamo curves zizwi uzikuye muri library zizewe; mudasobwa nini za quantum zishobora kubuvunagura umunsi umwe, ni yo mpamvu hategurwa algorithms za post-quantum."),
      ("Aina ya kisasa ya kriptografia ya funguo za umma inayotegemea hisabati ya mviringo wa elliptic inayotoa usalama mkubwa kwa funguo fupi zaidi kuliko RSA, hivyo ni ya haraka na nyepesi.", "Ni ya kawaida kwenye simu, vyeti vya TLS, funguo za SSH na sarafu za kidijitali (ECDSA, Ed25519). Chagua mviringo unaojulikana kutoka maktaba zinazoaminika; kompyuta kubwa za quantum zinaweza kuivunja siku moja, ndiyo maana algorithms za post-quantum zinasanifishwa.")),
    T("one-time-pad", "One-time pad", ["one-time pad", "one time pad", "otp cipher", "vernam cipher"], "crypto", "random key", {"fr": "Masque jetable", "sw": "One-time pad", "rw": "One-time pad"},
      ("A cipher that combines the message with a truly random key as long as the message, used only once. Used correctly it is mathematically unbreakable, but keys are hard to generate, share and never reuse.", "Rarely practical outside special cases. Do not confuse it with an OTP (one-time password) code sent to your phone, which is a different thing."),
      ("Un chiffre qui combine le message avec une clé vraiment aléatoire aussi longue que le message, utilisée une seule fois. Bien employé, il est mathématiquement incassable, mais les clés sont difficiles à générer, partager et ne jamais réutiliser.", "Rarement pratique hors cas spéciaux. Ne le confondez pas avec un code OTP (mot de passe à usage unique) reçu sur le téléphone, qui est autre chose."),
      ("Cipher ihuza ubutumwa n'urufunguzo rwa nyabyo rw'amahirwe rungana n'ubutumwa, rukoreshwa rimwe gusa. Rukoreshejwe neza ntirushobora kuvunagurwa mu mibare, ariko imfunguzo zigorana gukorwa, gusangizwa no kudasubira gukoreshwa.", "Si ikoreshwa kenshi hanze y'ibihe byihariye. Ntukayitiranye na kode ya OTP (ijambo ry'ibanga rikoreshwa rimwe) wohererezwa kuri telefone, ni ikindi kintu."),
      ("Cipher inayochanganya ujumbe na ufunguo wa nasibu halisi wenye urefu sawa na ujumbe, unaotumika mara moja tu. Ikitumika sawasawa haivunjiki kihisabati, lakini funguo ni ngumu kuzalisha, kushiriki na kutotumia tena.", "Mara chache ni ya vitendo nje ya hali maalum. Usiichanganye na msimbo wa OTP (nywila ya matumizi moja) unaotumwa kwa simu, ni kitu tofauti.")),
    T("hash-collision", "Hash collision", ["hash collision", "collision attack", "md5 collision", "sha-1 collision", "birthday attack"], "crypto", "matching fingerprints", {"fr": "Collision de hachage", "sw": "Mgongano wa hash", "rw": "Hash collision"},
      ("A collision is when two different inputs produce the same hash. Good hash functions make this practically impossible; weak ones (MD5, SHA-1) have been broken so attackers can craft colliding files.", "That is why MD5 and SHA-1 should not be used for signatures or integrity checks. Use SHA-256 or stronger, and for passwords use a slow password-hashing function such as bcrypt or Argon2."),
      ("Une collision, c'est quand deux entrées différentes donnent le même hachage. Les bonnes fonctions la rendent pratiquement impossible ; les faibles (MD5, SHA-1) ont été cassées et permettent de fabriquer des fichiers en collision.", "C'est pourquoi MD5 et SHA-1 ne doivent plus servir aux signatures ni aux contrôles d'intégrité. Utilisez SHA-256 ou plus, et pour les mots de passe une fonction lente comme bcrypt ou Argon2."),
      ("Collision ni iyo ibyinjijwe bibiri bitandukanye bitanga hash imwe. Hash functions nziza zituma bidashoboka mu by'ukuri; izidakomeye (MD5, SHA-1) zaravunaguwe, abashimusi bashobora gukora dosiye zihuje.", "Ni yo mpamvu MD5 na SHA-1 zitagomba gukoreshwa mu masinya cyangwa kugenzura ubuziranenge. Koresha SHA-256 cyangwa irenze, ku magambo y'ibanga ukoreshe function itinda nka bcrypt cyangwa Argon2."),
      ("Mgongano ni wakati ingizo mbili tofauti zinapozaa hash moja. Kazi nzuri za hash hufanya hili lisiwezekane kivitendo; dhaifu (MD5, SHA-1) zimevunjwa na washambuliaji wanaweza kutengeneza faili zinazogongana.", "Ndiyo maana MD5 na SHA-1 hazipaswi kutumika kwa sahihi au ukaguzi wa uadilifu. Tumia SHA-256 au zaidi, na kwa nywila tumia kazi ya polepole kama bcrypt au Argon2.")),
    T("password-hashing-pepper", "Pepper, bcrypt and Argon2", ["pepper", "password pepper", "bcrypt", "argon2", "pbkdf2", "key stretching", "password hashing"], "crypto", "password security lock", {"fr": "Poivre, bcrypt et Argon2", "sw": "Pepper, bcrypt na Argon2", "rw": "Pepper, bcrypt na Argon2"},
      ("Safe password storage uses a slow hash (bcrypt, Argon2, PBKDF2) so each guess is costly, a unique salt per password, and sometimes a secret “pepper” kept outside the database.", "Websites should never store plain or fast-hashed passwords. As a user, you cannot see this, so use unique passwords and MFA so that a breach of one site does not expose your other accounts."),
      ("Un stockage sûr des mots de passe utilise un hachage lent (bcrypt, Argon2, PBKDF2) pour que chaque essai coûte cher, un sel unique par mot de passe et parfois un « poivre » secret gardé hors de la base.", "Un site ne doit jamais stocker de mots de passe en clair ou hachés rapidement. Utilisateur, vous ne le voyez pas : utilisez des mots de passe uniques et la MFA pour qu'une fuite sur un site n'expose pas vos autres comptes."),
      ("Kubika amagambo y'ibanga neza bikoresha hash itinda (bcrypt, Argon2, PBKDF2) kugira ngo buri igerageza gutwara ikiguzi, salt yihariye kuri buri jambo, rimwe na rimwe na «pepper» y'ibanga ibitswe hanze ya database.", "Urubuga ntirugomba kubika amagambo y'ibanga mu nyandiko isanzwe cyangwa hash yihuta. Nk'ukoresha ntubibona: koresha amagambo y'ibanga yihariye na MFA kugira ngo kumeneka ku rubuga rumwe bitagaragaza izindi konti."),
      ("Uhifadhi salama wa nywila hutumia hash ya polepole (bcrypt, Argon2, PBKDF2) ili kila jaribio liwe ghali, salt ya kipekee kwa kila nywila, na wakati mwingine «pepper» ya siri inayowekwa nje ya hifadhidata.", "Tovuti hazipaswi kamwe kuhifadhi nywila wazi au hash za haraka. Kama mtumiaji huwezi kuona hili, hivyo tumia nywila za kipekee na MFA ili uvujaji wa tovuti moja usifichue akaunti zako nyingine.")),
    T("zero-knowledge-proof", "Zero-knowledge proof", ["zero-knowledge proof", "zero knowledge proof", "zkp", "zk-snark", "zk proof"], "crypto", "proving without revealing", {"fr": "Preuve à divulgation nulle de connaissance", "sw": "Uthibitisho wa zero-knowledge", "rw": "Zero-knowledge proof"},
      ("A way to prove that something is true (for example that you know a password or are over 18) without revealing the secret or the underlying data itself.", "Used to improve privacy in identity checks, login and some blockchains. It lets a service verify a claim without collecting your documents, which reduces what can be breached."),
      ("Une manière de prouver qu'une chose est vraie (par exemple connaître un mot de passe ou avoir plus de 18 ans) sans révéler le secret ni les données elles-mêmes.", "Utilisée pour améliorer la vie privée dans les vérifications d'identité, la connexion et certaines blockchains. Elle permet à un service de vérifier une affirmation sans collecter vos documents, ce qui réduit ce qui peut fuiter."),
      ("Uburyo bwo kwerekana ko ikintu ari ukuri (urugero ko uzi ijambo ry'ibanga cyangwa ufite imyaka irenga 18) udatanze ibanga cyangwa amakuru ubwayo.", "Bukoreshwa mu kunoza ibanga mu gusuzuma umwirondoro, kwinjira na blockchains zimwe. Butuma serivisi igenzura ibyo uvuga itabitse inyandiko zawe, bigabanya ibyashobora kumeneka."),
      ("Njia ya kuthibitisha kuwa kitu ni kweli (mfano unajua nywila au una zaidi ya miaka 18) bila kufichua siri au data yenyewe.", "Hutumika kuboresha faragha kwenye ukaguzi wa utambulisho, kuingia na baadhi ya blockchain. Inaruhusu huduma kuthibitisha dai bila kukusanya nyaraka zako, kupunguza kinachoweza kuvuja.")),
    T("homomorphic-encryption", "Homomorphic encryption", ["homomorphic encryption", "fully homomorphic encryption", "fhe", "compute on encrypted data"], "crypto", "encrypted computation", {"fr": "Chiffrement homomorphe", "sw": "Usimbaji wa homomorphic", "rw": "Homomorphic encryption"},
      ("An advanced form of encryption that lets a computer calculate on data while it stays encrypted, so the cloud provider never sees the readable data.", "Still slow and used in special cases (private analytics, health or finance research). It shows the direction of privacy-preserving computing alongside confidential computing and secure enclaves."),
      ("Forme avancée de chiffrement qui permet à un ordinateur de calculer sur des données restant chiffrées, de sorte que le fournisseur cloud ne voit jamais les données lisibles.", "Encore lente et utilisée dans des cas particuliers (analyses privées, recherche en santé ou finance). Elle montre la direction du calcul préservant la vie privée, avec l'informatique confidentielle et les enclaves sécurisées."),
      ("Uburyo bwa none bwa encryption butuma mudasobwa ibarira ku makuru akiri afunze, bityo utanga cloud ntiyigera abona amakuru asomeka.", "Biracyatinda kandi bikoreshwa mu bihe byihariye (isesengura rya bwite, ubushakashatsi mu buzima cyangwa imari). Bigaragaza icyerekezo cy'ibarura rirengera ibanga, hamwe na confidential computing na secure enclaves."),
      ("Aina ya hali ya juu ya usimbaji inayoruhusu kompyuta kukokotoa kwenye data ikiwa imesimbwa, hivyo mtoa huduma wa cloud haoni data inayosomeka.", "Bado ni polepole na hutumika katika hali maalum (uchambuzi wa faragha, utafiti wa afya au fedha). Inaonyesha mwelekeo wa kompyuta inayolinda faragha pamoja na confidential computing na secure enclaves.")),
    T("blockchain-security", "Blockchain and smart-contract security", ["blockchain", "blockchain security", "smart contract", "smart contract vulnerability", "reentrancy", "51% attack", "defi hack"], "appsec", "blockchain network", {"fr": "Sécurité de la blockchain et des contrats intelligents", "sw": "Usalama wa blockchain na smart contract", "rw": "Umutekano wa blockchain na smart contract"},
      ("A blockchain is a shared ledger that is very hard to alter. Weak points are usually not the chain itself but bugs in smart contracts (self-executing code), stolen private keys, exchanges and scams.", "Never share your seed phrase, check contracts and websites before approving, use hardware wallets for large amounts, and remember that crypto transactions are normally irreversible."),
      ("Une blockchain est un registre partagé très difficile à modifier. Les points faibles ne sont généralement pas la chaîne elle-même mais les bogues des contrats intelligents (code auto-exécutable), les clés privées volées, les plateformes d'échange et les arnaques.", "Ne partagez jamais votre phrase de récupération, vérifiez contrats et sites avant d'approuver, utilisez un portefeuille matériel pour les gros montants et rappelez-vous que les transactions crypto sont en général irréversibles."),
      ("Blockchain ni igitabo gisangiwe bigoye cyane guhindura. Intege nke akenshi si urunigi ubwarwo ahubwo ni amakosa muri smart contracts (code ikora yonyine), imfunguzo bwite zibwe, amasoko n'uburiganya.", "Ntugasangize seed phrase yawe, genzura contracts n'imbuga mbere yo kwemeza, koresha hardware wallet ku mafaranga menshi kandi wibuke ko ibikorwa bya crypto bisanzwe bidasubirwamo."),
      ("Blockchain ni leja ya pamoja ngumu sana kubadilisha. Pointi dhaifu mara nyingi si mnyororo wenyewe bali hitilafu kwenye smart contracts (msimbo unaojitekeleza), funguo za faragha zilizoibwa, soko na ulaghai.", "Kamwe usishiriki seed phrase yako, kagua contracts na tovuti kabla ya kuidhinisha, tumia pochi ya vifaa kwa kiasi kikubwa na kumbuka miamala ya crypto kwa kawaida haibatilishwi.")),
    T("nat", "NAT (network address translation)", ["nat", "network address translation", "port forwarding", "cgnat", "private ip address"], "network", "home router", {"fr": "NAT (traduction d'adresses réseau)", "sw": "NAT (tafsiri ya anwani za mtandao)", "rw": "NAT (guhindura aderesi z'umuyoboro)"},
      ("NAT lets many devices on a private network (home or office) share one public IP address by rewriting addresses on traffic going in and out of the router.", "It hides internal devices from direct internet connections, a small side benefit for security, but it is not a firewall. Avoid port forwarding to devices unless needed and protected."),
      ("Le NAT permet à de nombreux appareils d'un réseau privé (maison ou bureau) de partager une adresse IP publique en réécrivant les adresses du trafic entrant et sortant du routeur.", "Il masque les appareils internes aux connexions directes depuis internet, petit avantage de sécurité, mais ce n'est pas un pare-feu. Évitez la redirection de ports vers des appareils sauf si nécessaire et protégés."),
      ("NAT ituma ibikoresho byinshi biri mu muyoboro wihariye (urugo cyangwa ibiro) bisangira aderesi imwe ya IP rusange ihindura aderesi z'amakuru yinjira n'asohoka muri router.", "Ihisha ibikoresho by'imbere ku bihuza bitaziguye na interineti, inyungu nto mu mutekano, ariko si firewall. Irinde port forwarding ku bikoresho keretse bikenewe kandi birinzwe."),
      ("NAT huruhusu vifaa vingi kwenye mtandao wa faragha (nyumbani au ofisini) kushiriki anwani moja ya IP ya umma kwa kuandika upya anwani za trafiki inayoingia na kutoka kwenye router.", "Huficha vifaa vya ndani na miunganisho ya moja kwa moja kutoka mtandaoni, faida ndogo ya usalama, lakini si firewall. Epuka port forwarding kwa vifaa isipokuwa ni lazima na vimelindwa.")),
    T("osi-tcpip-model", "OSI and TCP/IP models", ["osi model", "tcp/ip", "tcp ip model", "network layers", "osi layers", "seven layers"], "network", "network cables", {"fr": "Modèles OSI et TCP/IP", "sw": "Miundo ya OSI na TCP/IP", "rw": "Ingero za OSI na TCP/IP"},
      ("Layered descriptions of how networks work. OSI has 7 layers (physical, data link, network, transport, session, presentation, application); TCP/IP simplifies this to 4 or 5.", "Security people use layers to place controls and name attacks: ARP spoofing (layer 2), IP spoofing (3), SYN flood (4), phishing and SQL injection (7). Defence in depth means protecting several layers."),
      ("Descriptions en couches du fonctionnement des réseaux. OSI compte 7 couches (physique, liaison, réseau, transport, session, présentation, application) ; TCP/IP les simplifie en 4 ou 5.", "Les spécialistes les utilisent pour placer les contrôles et nommer les attaques : usurpation ARP (couche 2), IP (3), SYN flood (4), phishing et injection SQL (7). La défense en profondeur protège plusieurs couches."),
      ("Ibisobanuro by'ibyiciro by'uko imiyoboro ikora. OSI ifite ibyiciro 7 (physical, data link, network, transport, session, presentation, application); TCP/IP ibigabanya kuri 4 cyangwa 5.", "Abakora mu mutekano babikoresha mu gushyira ingamba no kwita ibitero amazina: ARP spoofing (icyiciro 2), IP spoofing (3), SYN flood (4), phishing na SQL injection (7). Defence in depth irinda ibyiciro byinshi."),
      ("Maelezo ya tabaka ya jinsi mitandao inavyofanya kazi. OSI ina tabaka 7 (physical, data link, network, transport, session, presentation, application); TCP/IP hurahisisha kuwa 4 au 5.", "Wataalamu wa usalama hutumia tabaka kuweka udhibiti na kutaja mashambulizi: ARP spoofing (tabaka 2), IP spoofing (3), SYN flood (4), hadaa na SQL injection (7). Defence in depth hulinda tabaka nyingi.")),
    T("ddos-mitigation", "DDoS mitigation", ["ddos mitigation", "scrubbing centre", "scrubbing center", "anycast", "traffic scrubbing", "cdn protection"], "network", "traffic filtering", {"fr": "Atténuation DDoS", "sw": "Kupunguza DDoS", "rw": "Kugabanya ingaruka za DDoS"},
      ("Ways to keep a service online during a flood of fake traffic: spreading it over many servers (CDN, anycast), filtering bad traffic in “scrubbing centres”, rate limiting and capacity planning.", "Small sites can use a reputable CDN or DDoS-protection service, keep an incident plan and avoid exposing origin server addresses. Never pay extortion demands that threaten a DDoS."),
      ("Moyens de garder un service en ligne pendant un déluge de faux trafic : le répartir sur de nombreux serveurs (CDN, anycast), filtrer le trafic malveillant dans des « centres de nettoyage », limiter les débits et planifier la capacité.", "Les petits sites peuvent utiliser un CDN ou service anti-DDoS réputé, avoir un plan d'incident et ne pas exposer l'adresse du serveur d'origine. Ne payez jamais une extorsion menaçant d'un DDoS."),
      ("Uburyo bwo gutuma serivisi ikomeza gukora mu gihe cy'urujya n'uruza rw'ibinyoma: kuyikwirakwiza kuri seriveri nyinshi (CDN, anycast), gushungura urujya n'uruza rubi mu «scrubbing centres», rate limiting no gutegura ubushobozi.", "Imbuga nto zishobora gukoresha CDN cyangwa serivisi yizewe irwanya DDoS, kugira gahunda y'ibitero no kudatangaza aderesi ya seriveri y'ibanze. Ntuzigere wishyura abakwaka amafaranga bakubwira DDoS."),
      ("Njia za kuweka huduma mtandaoni wakati wa mafuriko ya trafiki bandia: kuisambaza kwenye seva nyingi (CDN, anycast), kuchuja trafiki mbaya kwenye «vituo vya kusafisha», kikomo cha maombi na mipango ya uwezo.", "Tovuti ndogo zinaweza kutumia CDN au huduma ya kuaminika ya kinga ya DDoS, kuwa na mpango wa matukio na kutofichua anwani ya seva asili. Kamwe usilipe madai ya fidia yanayotishia DDoS.")),
    T("security-posture", "Security posture", ["security posture", "cyber posture", "posture assessment", "security maturity"], "governance", "security dashboard", {"fr": "Posture de sécurité", "sw": "Hali ya usalama (security posture)", "rw": "Imiterere y'umutekano (security posture)"},
      ("The overall strength of an organisation's cyber defences: its policies, technology, people, processes and how ready it is to prevent, detect and respond to attacks.", "Measured through risk assessments, audits, penetration tests, maturity models and metrics such as patch coverage or time to detect. Improve it step by step, starting with the biggest risks."),
      ("La solidité globale des défenses cyber d'une organisation : politiques, technologies, personnes, processus et sa capacité à prévenir, détecter et répondre aux attaques.", "Mesurée par évaluations de risques, audits, tests d'intrusion, modèles de maturité et indicateurs comme la couverture des correctifs ou le délai de détection. On l'améliore pas à pas, en commençant par les plus gros risques."),
      ("Imbaraga rusange z'ingamba z'umutekano w'ikigo: politiki, ikoranabuhanga, abantu, uburyo bw'imikorere n'uko cyiteguye gukumira, gutahura no gusubiza ibitero.", "Bipimwa hakoreshejwe isuzuma ry'ibyago, audits, penetration tests, maturity models n'ibipimo nka patch coverage cyangwa igihe cyo gutahura. Gitunganywa intambwe ku yindi, uhereye ku byago bikomeye."),
      ("Nguvu ya jumla ya ulinzi wa mtandao wa shirika: sera, teknolojia, watu, michakato na utayari wake wa kuzuia, kugundua na kujibu mashambulizi.", "Hupimwa kwa tathmini za hatari, ukaguzi, majaribio ya kupenya, mifano ya ukomavu na vipimo kama ufunikaji wa viraka au muda wa kugundua. Huboreshwa hatua kwa hatua, kuanzia hatari kubwa.")),
    T("soc-2", "SOC 2", ["soc 2", "soc2", "soc 2 report", "service organization control"], "governance", "audit report", {"fr": "SOC 2", "sw": "SOC 2", "rw": "SOC 2"},
      ("An independent audit report (from the US AICPA framework) showing that a service provider has controls for security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality and privacy. Type I checks design; Type II checks operation over time.", "Companies ask cloud and software vendors for a SOC 2 report as part of third-party risk checks. It is evidence of good practice, not a guarantee that a vendor can never be breached."),
      ("Rapport d'audit indépendant (du cadre américain AICPA) montrant qu'un prestataire a des contrôles de sécurité, disponibilité, intégrité des traitements, confidentialité et vie privée. Le Type I vérifie la conception ; le Type II le fonctionnement dans la durée.", "Les entreprises demandent un rapport SOC 2 aux fournisseurs cloud et logiciels dans l'évaluation des risques tiers. C'est une preuve de bonnes pratiques, pas une garantie qu'un fournisseur ne sera jamais piraté."),
      ("Raporo y'igenzura yigenga (iva muri AICPA yo muri Amerika) yerekana ko utanga serivisi afite ingamba z'umutekano, kuboneka, ubuziranenge bw'ibikorwa, ibanga n'ubuzima bwite. Type I igenzura imiterere; Type II igenzura imikorere mu gihe.", "Ibigo bisaba raporo ya SOC 2 abatanga cloud na porogaramu mu isuzuma ry'ibyago by'abandi bantu. Ni ikimenyetso cy'imikorere myiza, si ingwate ko utanga serivisi atazigera ameneka."),
      ("Ripoti ya ukaguzi huru (kutoka mfumo wa AICPA wa Marekani) inayoonyesha mtoa huduma ana udhibiti wa usalama, upatikanaji, uadilifu wa uchakataji, usiri na faragha. Type I hukagua muundo; Type II hukagua utendaji kwa muda.", "Makampuni huomba ripoti ya SOC 2 kutoka kwa wauzaji wa cloud na programu kama sehemu ya ukaguzi wa hatari za wahusika wa tatu. Ni ushahidi wa mazoea mazuri, si dhamana kuwa muuzaji hatadukuliwa.")),
    T("hipaa", "HIPAA", ["hipaa", "health insurance portability and accountability act", "health data law", "medical privacy law"], "governance", "medical records privacy", {"fr": "HIPAA", "sw": "HIPAA", "rw": "HIPAA"},
      ("A US law that sets rules for protecting patients' health information (security, privacy and breach notification) for healthcare providers, insurers and their service partners.", "Outside the US other laws apply (for example Rwanda's data protection law covers health data as sensitive data). The common principles are the same: collect little, restrict access, encrypt, log access and report breaches."),
      ("Loi américaine qui fixe les règles de protection des informations de santé des patients (sécurité, confidentialité, notification des violations) pour les prestataires de soins, assureurs et leurs partenaires.", "Hors des États-Unis d'autres lois s'appliquent (par exemple la loi rwandaise sur la protection des données traite les données de santé comme sensibles). Les principes communs : collecter peu, restreindre l'accès, chiffrer, journaliser les accès et signaler les violations."),
      ("Itegeko ryo muri Amerika rishyiraho amategeko yo kurinda amakuru y'ubuzima y'abarwayi (umutekano, ibanga no kumenyesha amakuru yamenetse) ku batanga ubuvuzi, ubwishingizi n'abafatanyabikorwa babo.", "Hanze ya Amerika andi mategeko arakurikizwa (urugero itegeko ry'u Rwanda ryo kurengera amakuru bwite rifata amakuru y'ubuzima nk'amakuru yihariye). Amahame rusange ni amwe: gukusanya make, kugabanya abayageraho, encryption, kwandika abayageraho no kumenyesha amakuru yamenetse."),
      ("Sheria ya Marekani inayoweka kanuni za kulinda taarifa za afya za wagonjwa (usalama, faragha na taarifa za uvujaji) kwa watoa huduma za afya, bima na washirika wao.", "Nje ya Marekani sheria nyingine hutumika (mfano sheria ya Rwanda ya ulinzi wa data huchukulia data za afya kama nyeti). Kanuni za pamoja ni zilezile: kukusanya kidogo, kudhibiti ufikiaji, kusimba, kurekodi ufikiaji na kuripoti uvujaji.")),
    T("nis2", "NIS2 Directive", ["nis2", "nis 2", "nis2 directive", "network and information security directive"], "governance", "european union flag", {"fr": "Directive NIS2", "sw": "Maelekezo ya NIS2", "rw": "Itegeko-ngenga rya NIS2"},
      ("A European Union law (in force since 2023) that requires many essential and important organisations to manage cyber risk, report serious incidents quickly and hold leaders accountable.", "It affects any company that serves EU customers or supplies EU firms. It is a model of how governments are moving from voluntary advice to legal duties for risk management, supply-chain security and incident reporting."),
      ("Loi de l'Union européenne (en vigueur depuis 2023) qui oblige de nombreuses organisations essentielles et importantes à gérer le risque cyber, déclarer rapidement les incidents graves et engager la responsabilité des dirigeants.", "Elle touche toute entreprise servant des clients de l'UE ou fournissant des sociétés de l'UE. Elle illustre le passage de conseils volontaires à des obligations légales de gestion des risques, de sécurité de la chaîne d'approvisionnement et de déclaration d'incidents."),
      ("Itegeko ry'Umuryango w'u Burayi (rikurikizwa kuva 2023) risaba ibigo byinshi by'ingenzi gucunga ibyago bya cyber, kumenyesha vuba ibitero bikomeye no kubazwa inshingano abayobozi.", "Rigira ingaruka ku kigo cyose gikorera abakiriya b'u Burayi cyangwa gitanga ibicuruzwa ku bigo by'u Burayi. Ni urugero rw'uko za leta zikomoka ku nama z'ubushake zijya ku nshingano z'amategeko mu gucunga ibyago, umutekano w'itangwa n'itangazwa ry'ibitero."),
      ("Sheria ya Umoja wa Ulaya (inayotumika tangu 2023) inayohitaji mashirika mengi muhimu kusimamia hatari za mtandao, kuripoti matukio makubwa haraka na kuwajibisha viongozi.", "Inaathiri kampuni yoyote inayohudumia wateja wa EU au kusambaza makampuni ya EU. Ni mfano wa jinsi serikali zinavyohama kutoka ushauri wa hiari hadi wajibu wa kisheria wa usimamizi wa hatari, usalama wa ugavi na kuripoti matukio.")),
    T("data-sovereignty", "Data sovereignty and residency", ["data sovereignty", "data residency", "data localisation", "data localization", "cross-border data transfer", "data transfer"], "privacy", "world map data flows", {"fr": "Souveraineté et résidence des données", "sw": "Mamlaka na makazi ya data", "rw": "Ubusugire n'aho amakuru abitswe"},
      ("Data sovereignty means data is subject to the laws of the country where it is stored or collected; data residency is the physical location where it is kept. Some laws limit sending personal data abroad.", "Organisations should know where their cloud data lives, use contracts and safeguards for cross-border transfers and follow national rules such as Rwanda's data protection law when moving personal data."),
      ("La souveraineté des données signifie qu'elles relèvent des lois du pays où elles sont stockées ou collectées ; la résidence des données est le lieu physique de leur conservation. Certaines lois limitent l'envoi de données personnelles à l'étranger.", "Les organisations doivent savoir où se trouvent leurs données cloud, utiliser des contrats et garanties pour les transferts transfrontaliers et suivre les règles nationales, comme la loi rwandaise sur la protection des données, pour déplacer des données personnelles."),
      ("Ubusugire bw'amakuru busobanura ko amakuru agengwa n'amategeko y'igihugu ari kubikwamo cyangwa yakusanyirijwemo; aho amakuru abitse ni ahantu nyirizina ari. Andi mategeko agabanya kohereza amakuru bwite mu mahanga.", "Ibigo bigomba kumenya aho amakuru yabyo ya cloud abitse, gukoresha amasezerano n'ingamba ku kohereza amakuru mu mahanga no gukurikiza amategeko y'igihugu nk'itegeko ry'u Rwanda ryo kurengera amakuru bwite iyo bimuye amakuru bwite."),
      ("Mamlaka ya data inamaanisha data iko chini ya sheria za nchi inapohifadhiwa au kukusanywa; makazi ya data ni mahali pa kimwili inapohifadhiwa. Sheria zingine hupunguza kutuma data binafsi nje ya nchi.", "Mashirika yajue data zao za cloud ziko wapi, yatumie mikataba na ulinzi kwa uhamishaji wa mipakani na kufuata kanuni za kitaifa kama sheria ya Rwanda ya ulinzi wa data wanapohamisha data binafsi.")),
    T("controller-processor-dpia", "Data controller, processor and DPIA", ["data controller", "data processor", "dpia", "data protection impact assessment", "dpo", "data protection officer"], "privacy", "data protection paperwork", {"fr": "Responsable de traitement, sous-traitant et AIPD", "sw": "Mdhibiti data, mchakataji na DPIA", "rw": "Utegeka amakuru, utunganya n'DPIA"},
      ("A data controller decides why and how personal data is used; a processor handles it on the controller's behalf. A DPIA (data protection impact assessment) checks the privacy risks of a new project before it starts; a DPO advises on compliance.", "Typical duties: collect only what is needed, tell people how data is used, protect it, limit retention, honour people's rights and report breaches. Check the exact wording of your national law (such as Rwanda's) for local duties."),
      ("Le responsable de traitement décide pourquoi et comment les données personnelles sont utilisées ; le sous-traitant les traite pour son compte. Une AIPD (DPIA) évalue les risques pour la vie privée d'un nouveau projet avant son démarrage ; le DPO conseille sur la conformité.", "Devoirs courants : ne collecter que le nécessaire, informer, protéger, limiter la conservation, respecter les droits des personnes et signaler les violations. Vérifiez la loi nationale exacte (comme celle du Rwanda) pour les obligations locales."),
      ("Utegeka amakuru (controller) afata icyemezo cy'impamvu n'uko amakuru bwite akoreshwa; utunganya (processor) ayakoresha mu mwanya we. DPIA ni isuzuma ry'ibyago ku ibanga mbere y'uko umushinga utangira; DPO atanga inama ku kubahiriza amategeko.", "Inshingano zisanzwe: gukusanya ibikenewe gusa, kumenyesha uko akoreshwa, kuyarinda, kugabanya igihe abikwa, kubahiriza uburenganzira bw'abantu no kumenyesha ayamenetse. Reba amagambo nyayo y'itegeko ry'igihugu (nk'iry'u Rwanda) ku nshingano zo mu gihugu."),
      ("Mdhibiti wa data (controller) huamua kwa nini na jinsi data binafsi zinatumika; mchakataji (processor) huzishughulikia kwa niaba yake. DPIA hukagua hatari za faragha za mradi mpya kabla haujaanza; DPO hushauri kuhusu utiifu.", "Wajibu wa kawaida: kukusanya kinachohitajika tu, kueleza matumizi, kuilinda, kupunguza muda wa kuhifadhi, kuheshimu haki za watu na kuripoti uvujaji. Angalia maneno halisi ya sheria ya taifa (kama ya Rwanda) kwa wajibu wa ndani.")),
    T("cookie-consent", "Cookie consent and tracking", ["cookie consent", "cookie banner", "tracking cookies", "third-party cookies", "web tracking", "tracking pixel"], "privacy", "website cookie banner", {"fr": "Consentement aux cookies et traçage", "sw": "Ridhaa ya cookies na ufuatiliaji", "rw": "Uruhushya rwa cookies no gukurikirana"},
      ("Cookies and tracking pixels let websites and advertisers recognise you across pages and sites. Privacy laws usually require clear consent for non-essential tracking.", "You can reduce tracking by rejecting non-essential cookies, using a privacy-friendly browser, blocking third-party cookies and reviewing app permissions. Be wary of banners that make “reject” hard to find."),
      ("Les cookies et pixels de suivi permettent aux sites et annonceurs de vous reconnaître d'une page ou d'un site à l'autre. Les lois sur la vie privée exigent en général un consentement clair pour le suivi non essentiel.", "Vous pouvez réduire le suivi en refusant les cookies non essentiels, en utilisant un navigateur respectueux de la vie privée, en bloquant les cookies tiers et en revoyant les permissions des applications. Méfiez-vous des bandeaux où « refuser » est caché."),
      ("Cookies na tracking pixels bituma imbuga n'abamamaza bakumenya ku mpapuro n'imbuga zitandukanye. Amategeko y'ibanga akenshi asaba uruhushya rusobanutse ku gukurikirana kutari ngombwa.", "Ushobora kugabanya gukurikirana wanga cookies zitari ngombwa, ukoresha browser irengera ibanga, ukabuza cookies z'abandi no gusuzuma uburenganzira bwa porogaramu. Witondere ibimenyetso bigora kubona «anga»."),
      ("Cookies na tracking pixels huruhusu tovuti na watangazaji kukutambua kwenye kurasa na tovuti mbalimbali. Sheria za faragha kwa kawaida zinahitaji ridhaa wazi kwa ufuatiliaji usio wa lazima.", "Unaweza kupunguza ufuatiliaji kwa kukataa cookies zisizo za lazima, kutumia kivinjari rafiki kwa faragha, kuzuia cookies za wahusika wengine na kukagua ruhusa za programu. Kuwa makini na mabango yanayoficha «kataa».")),
    T("mobile-threat-defense", "Mobile threat defense (MTD)", ["mobile threat defense", "mtd", "mobile security app", "phone antivirus", "mobile endpoint security"], "cloud", "smartphone security shield", {"fr": "Défense contre les menaces mobiles (MTD)", "sw": "Ulinzi dhidi ya vitisho vya simu (MTD)", "rw": "Kurinda iterabwoba kuri telefone (MTD)"},
      ("Security software that watches phones and tablets for malicious apps, risky Wi-Fi, phishing links and operating-system weaknesses, and can alert or block access to company data.", "Individuals benefit more from basics: official stores only, system updates, screen lock, minimal permissions and Play Protect or the iPhone's built-in defences. Organisations pair MTD with device management (MDM)."),
      ("Logiciel de sécurité qui surveille téléphones et tablettes à la recherche d'applications malveillantes, de Wi-Fi risqué, de liens de phishing et de faiblesses du système, et peut alerter ou bloquer l'accès aux données de l'entreprise.", "Les particuliers gagnent davantage avec les bases : boutiques officielles, mises à jour, verrouillage d'écran, permissions minimales et Play Protect ou les défenses intégrées d'iPhone. Les organisations associent MTD et gestion des appareils (MDM)."),
      ("Porogaramu y'umutekano ikurikirana telefone na tablets ishaka porogaramu mbi, Wi-Fi ifite ibyago, amahuza ya phishing n'intege nke za sisitemu, ishobora kumenyesha cyangwa guhagarika kugera ku makuru y'ikigo.", "Abantu ku giti cyabo bunguka cyane ku by'ibanze: amaduka yemewe gusa, ivugurura rya sisitemu, gufunga ecran, uburenganzira bukeya na Play Protect cyangwa uburinzi bwa iPhone. Ibigo bihuza MTD na MDM."),
      ("Programu ya usalama inayofuatilia simu na tablet kutafuta programu hasidi, Wi-Fi hatari, viungo vya hadaa na udhaifu wa mfumo, na inaweza kutahadharisha au kuzuia ufikiaji wa data za kampuni.", "Watu binafsi hufaidika zaidi na misingi: maduka rasmi tu, masasisho ya mfumo, kufunga skrini, ruhusa ndogo na Play Protect au kinga zilizojengewa ndani ya iPhone. Mashirika huunganisha MTD na usimamizi wa vifaa (MDM).")),
    T("firmware-uefi-security", "Firmware, BIOS and UEFI security", ["firmware", "bios", "uefi", "firmware attack", "firmware update", "bios password", "firmware security"], "cloud", "computer motherboard", {"fr": "Sécurité du firmware, BIOS et UEFI", "sw": "Usalama wa firmware, BIOS na UEFI", "rw": "Umutekano wa firmware, BIOS na UEFI"},
      ("Firmware is the low-level software stored on a device (BIOS/UEFI on PCs, router and camera firmware) that runs before the operating system. Malware in firmware is hard to detect and survives reinstalling the system.", "Defences: install firmware updates from the manufacturer only, enable Secure Boot and a TPM, set a firmware password, and replace routers and devices that no longer receive updates."),
      ("Le firmware est le logiciel de bas niveau stocké dans un appareil (BIOS/UEFI des PC, firmware de routeur ou de caméra) qui s'exécute avant le système d'exploitation. Un malware dans le firmware est difficile à détecter et survit à la réinstallation du système.", "Défenses : installer uniquement les mises à jour du fabricant, activer Secure Boot et un TPM, définir un mot de passe firmware et remplacer routeurs et appareils qui ne reçoivent plus de mises à jour."),
      ("Firmware ni porogaramu yo ku rwego rwo hasi ibitswe mu gikoresho (BIOS/UEFI ya PC, firmware ya router na kamera) ikora mbere ya sisitemu y'imikorere. Malware muri firmware igorana gutahurwa kandi irokoka gushyiraho sisitemu bundi bushya.", "Kwirinda: shyiraho ivugurura ry'uruganda gusa, fungura Secure Boot na TPM, shyiraho ijambo ry'ibanga rya firmware kandi usimbuze router n'ibikoresho bidacyivugurura."),
      ("Firmware ni programu ya kiwango cha chini iliyohifadhiwa kwenye kifaa (BIOS/UEFI ya PC, firmware ya router na kamera) inayoendeshwa kabla ya mfumo wa uendeshaji. Programu hasidi kwenye firmware ni ngumu kugundua na hubaki hata ukisakinisha mfumo upya.", "Ulinzi: sakinisha masasisho ya mtengenezaji pekee, washa Secure Boot na TPM, weka nenosiri la firmware na ubadilishe router na vifaa visivyopata masasisho tena.")),
    T("secure-enclave-tee", "Secure enclave and trusted execution environment", ["secure enclave", "trusted execution environment", "tee", "confidential computing", "arm trustzone", "intel sgx"], "cloud", "protected chip", {"fr": "Enclave sécurisée et environnement d'exécution de confiance", "sw": "Secure enclave na mazingira ya utekelezaji yanayoaminika", "rw": "Secure enclave na TEE"},
      ("A protected area inside a processor (a TEE or secure enclave) where sensitive code and data, such as biometric templates or encryption keys, run isolated even from the main operating system.", "It is why fingerprints and payment keys on modern phones are hard to steal. “Confidential computing” applies the same idea in the cloud so that even the provider cannot read data in use."),
      ("Zone protégée dans un processeur (TEE ou enclave sécurisée) où code et données sensibles, comme les modèles biométriques ou clés de chiffrement, s'exécutent isolés même du système d'exploitation principal.", "C'est pourquoi les empreintes et clés de paiement des téléphones modernes sont difficiles à voler. L'« informatique confidentielle » applique la même idée dans le cloud pour que même le fournisseur ne lise pas les données en cours d'usage."),
      ("Agace kirinzwe imbere muri processor (TEE cyangwa secure enclave) aho code n'amakuru y'ingenzi, nk'ibiranga umubiri cyangwa imfunguzo za encryption, bikorera byitaruye na sisitemu y'imikorere nkuru.", "Ni yo mpamvu ibikumwe n'imfunguzo zo kwishyura ku matelefone ya none bigoye kwibwa. «Confidential computing» ikoresha igitekerezo kimwe muri cloud kugira ngo n'utanga serivisi atasoma amakuru akoreshwa."),
      ("Eneo lililolindwa ndani ya processor (TEE au secure enclave) ambapo msimbo na data nyeti, kama violezo vya biometriki au funguo za usimbaji, hufanya kazi kwa kutengwa hata na mfumo mkuu wa uendeshaji.", "Ndiyo maana alama za vidole na funguo za malipo kwenye simu za kisasa ni ngumu kuibwa. «Confidential computing» hutumia wazo hilo kwenye cloud ili hata mtoa huduma asisome data zinazotumika.")),
    T("active-directory-kerberos", "Active Directory and Kerberos", ["active directory", "ad", "kerberos", "ntlm", "domain controller", "ldap directory"], "identity", "corporate network directory", {"fr": "Active Directory et Kerberos", "sw": "Active Directory na Kerberos", "rw": "Active Directory na Kerberos"},
      ("Active Directory is Microsoft's central directory that manages users, computers and permissions in most company networks. Kerberos and NTLM are the sign-in protocols behind it.", "Because it controls access to everything, it is a prime attacker target (see Kerberoasting, golden ticket, pass-the-hash). Defences: tiered admin accounts, MFA, patching domain controllers, disabling old protocols and monitoring sign-ins."),
      ("Active Directory est l'annuaire central de Microsoft qui gère utilisateurs, ordinateurs et permissions dans la plupart des réseaux d'entreprise. Kerberos et NTLM sont les protocoles de connexion sous-jacents.", "Comme il contrôle l'accès à tout, c'est une cible privilégiée (voir Kerberoasting, golden ticket, pass-the-hash). Défenses : comptes admin par niveaux, MFA, correctifs sur les contrôleurs de domaine, désactivation des anciens protocoles et surveillance des connexions."),
      ("Active Directory ni urutonde rukuru rwa Microsoft rucunga abakoresha, mudasobwa n'uburenganzira mu miyoboro myinshi y'ibigo. Kerberos na NTLM ni protocols zo kwinjira zibikoreshwamo.", "Kubera ko igenzura byose, ni cyo kintu cy'ibanze abashimusi bibasira (reba Kerberoasting, golden ticket, pass-the-hash). Kwirinda: konti za admin z'ibyiciro, MFA, kuvugurura domain controllers, guhagarika protocols zishaje no gukurikirana kwinjira."),
      ("Active Directory ni saraka kuu ya Microsoft inayosimamia watumiaji, kompyuta na ruhusa katika mitandao mingi ya makampuni. Kerberos na NTLM ni itifaki za kuingia nyuma yake.", "Kwa kuwa inadhibiti ufikiaji wa kila kitu, ni lengo kuu la washambuliaji (tazama Kerberoasting, golden ticket, pass-the-hash). Ulinzi: akaunti za admin za ngazi, MFA, viraka kwa domain controllers, kuzima itifaki za zamani na kufuatilia kuingia.")),
    T("vulnerability-scanners", "Vulnerability scanners (Nessus, OpenVAS, Nikto)", ["nessus", "openvas", "nikto", "vulnerability scanner", "qualys", "nuclei"], "operations", "security scan results", {"fr": "Scanners de vulnérabilités", "sw": "Vichanganuzi vya udhaifu", "rw": "Ibikoresho bisuzuma intege nke"},
      ("Tools that automatically check systems and websites for known weaknesses such as missing patches, weak settings and exposed services. Examples: Nessus, OpenVAS (open source), Nikto (web servers).", "Run them only on systems you own or have written permission to test. Treat results as a to-do list: fix high-risk findings first and re-scan, because scanners also give false positives."),
      ("Outils qui vérifient automatiquement systèmes et sites web à la recherche de faiblesses connues : correctifs manquants, mauvais réglages, services exposés. Exemples : Nessus, OpenVAS (libre), Nikto (serveurs web).", "Ne les lancez que sur des systèmes qui vous appartiennent ou avec autorisation écrite. Considérez les résultats comme une liste de tâches : corrigez d'abord les risques élevés et relancez, car les scanners donnent aussi des faux positifs."),
      ("Ibikoresho bisuzuma sisitemu n'imbuga mu buryo bwikora bishaka intege nke zizwi nko kubura ivugurura, igenamiterere ridakomeye na serivisi zigaragara. Ingero: Nessus, OpenVAS (ifunguye), Nikto (seriveri za web).", "Bikoreshe gusa ku bikoresho ari ibyawe cyangwa ufitiye uruhushya rwanditse. Fata ibisubizo nk'urutonde rw'imirimo: banza ukosore ibyago bikomeye, wongere usuzume, kuko scanners zitanga na false positives."),
      ("Zana zinazokagua mifumo na tovuti kiotomatiki kwa udhaifu unaojulikana kama viraka vilivyokosekana, mipangilio dhaifu na huduma zilizowazi. Mifano: Nessus, OpenVAS (chanzo huria), Nikto (seva za wavuti).", "Ziendeshe tu kwenye mifumo yako au ukiwa na ruhusa ya maandishi. Chukulia matokeo kama orodha ya kazi: rekebisha hatari kubwa kwanza na uchanganue tena, kwa sababu vichanganuzi pia hutoa false positives.")),
    T("password-testing-tools", "Password auditing tools (John the Ripper, Hashcat, Hydra)", ["john the ripper", "hashcat", "hydra", "password cracking tools", "password auditing", "password cracker"], "attacks", "password strength test", {"fr": "Outils d'audit de mots de passe", "sw": "Zana za kukagua nywila", "rw": "Ibikoresho byo gusuzuma amagambo y'ibanga"},
      ("Programs that guess passwords or test password hashes at high speed. Security teams use them (with permission) to find weak passwords; criminals use the same tools after a breach.", "The defence is the same for everyone: long unique passphrases, MFA, slow password hashing (bcrypt/Argon2), lockout and rate limits, and checking passwords against lists of known leaked passwords."),
      ("Programmes qui devinent des mots de passe ou testent des hachages à grande vitesse. Les équipes de sécurité les utilisent (avec autorisation) pour trouver les mots de passe faibles ; les criminels les utilisent aussi après une fuite.", "La défense est la même pour tous : phrases secrètes longues et uniques, MFA, hachage lent (bcrypt/Argon2), verrouillage et limitation des tentatives, et comparaison avec les listes de mots de passe déjà fuités."),
      ("Porogaramu zigerageza amagambo y'ibanga cyangwa zigerageza hash ku muvuduko mwinshi. Amatsinda y'umutekano arazikoresha (bafite uruhushya) kugira ngo bamenye amagambo y'ibanga adakomeye; abagizi ba nabi bakoresha izo nyine nyuma yo kumeneka.", "Uburyo bwo kwirinda ni bumwe kuri bose: interuro z'ibanga ndende kandi zihariye, MFA, hash itinda (bcrypt/Argon2), gufunga no kugabanya ibigeragezo no kugenzura ku mpapuro z'amagambo y'ibanga yamenetse."),
      ("Programu zinazokisia nywila au kujaribu hash kwa kasi kubwa. Timu za usalama huzitumia (kwa ruhusa) kutafuta nywila dhaifu; wahalifu hutumia zana zilezile baada ya uvujaji.", "Ulinzi ni ule ule kwa wote: nenosiri ndefu za kipekee, MFA, hash ya polepole (bcrypt/Argon2), kufunga akaunti na vikomo vya majaribio, na kulinganisha na orodha za nywila zilizovuja.")),
    T("internet-scanners-shodan", "Internet scanners (Shodan, Censys)", ["shodan", "censys", "internet scanner", "iot search engine", "exposed devices search"], "operations", "world map of devices", {"fr": "Moteurs de recherche d'appareils (Shodan, Censys)", "sw": "Injini za utafutaji wa vifaa (Shodan, Censys)", "rw": "Moteurs zishakisha ibikoresho (Shodan, Censys)"},
      ("Search engines that continuously scan the internet and list publicly reachable devices and services, such as webcams, routers, databases and industrial controllers, and what software they run.", "Defenders use them to find their own accidentally exposed assets; attackers use them to find easy targets. Check that your cameras, routers and databases are not directly reachable and use strong passwords."),
      ("Moteurs de recherche qui scannent en permanence internet et listent les appareils et services accessibles publiquement : webcams, routeurs, bases de données, automates industriels, et les logiciels qu'ils utilisent.", "Les défenseurs s'en servent pour trouver leurs propres actifs exposés par erreur ; les attaquants pour trouver des cibles faciles. Vérifiez que vos caméras, routeurs et bases ne sont pas accessibles directement et utilisez des mots de passe forts."),
      ("Moteurs zishakisha zisuzuma interineti ubudahwema zikandika ibikoresho na serivisi bigerwaho na bose, nka webcams, router, database n'ibikoresho by'inganda, n'ibikoreshwa muri byo.", "Abarinzi bazikoresha kubona ibyabo byagaragaye kubw'impanuka; abashimusi bazikoresha kubona intego zoroshye. Reba ko kamera, router na database byawe bidagerwaho mu buryo bweruye kandi ukoreshe amagambo y'ibanga akomeye."),
      ("Injini za utafutaji zinazochanganua mtandao kila wakati na kuorodhesha vifaa na huduma zinazofikika hadharani, kama kamera za wavuti, router, hifadhidata na vidhibiti vya viwanda, na programu wanazoendesha.", "Walinzi huzitumia kupata mali zao zilizofichuka kwa bahati mbaya; washambuliaji huzitumia kupata malengo rahisi. Hakikisha kamera, router na hifadhidata zako hazifikiki moja kwa moja na utumie nywila imara.")),
    T("malware-analysis-tools", "Malware analysis and reverse-engineering tools", ["ghidra", "ida pro", "virustotal", "any.run", "cuckoo sandbox", "malware analysis tools", "x64dbg", "disassembler"], "operations", "code analysis", {"fr": "Outils d'analyse de malwares et rétro-ingénierie", "sw": "Zana za kuchambua programu hasidi", "rw": "Ibikoresho byo gusesengura malware"},
      ("Tools analysts use to study suspicious files safely: online scanners and sandboxes (VirusTotal, Any.Run, Cuckoo) that run files and report behaviour, and disassemblers/debuggers (Ghidra, IDA, x64dbg) that read the code.", "Never open a suspicious file on your own device to “see what it does”. Upload it to a reputable scanner instead, remembering that anything you upload can become visible to others, so do not upload private documents."),
      ("Outils qu'utilisent les analystes pour étudier sans risque des fichiers suspects : scanners et bacs à sable en ligne (VirusTotal, Any.Run, Cuckoo) qui exécutent les fichiers et décrivent leur comportement, et désassembleurs/débogueurs (Ghidra, IDA, x64dbg) qui lisent le code.", "N'ouvrez jamais un fichier suspect sur votre appareil pour « voir ce qu'il fait ». Envoyez-le plutôt à un scanner réputé, en sachant que ce que vous envoyez peut devenir visible par d'autres : n'envoyez pas de documents privés."),
      ("Ibikoresho abasesenguzi bakoresha mu kwiga dosiye zikekwa mu buryo butekanye: scanners na sandboxes zo kuri interineti (VirusTotal, Any.Run, Cuckoo) zikoresha dosiye zikavuga imyitwarire, na disassemblers/debuggers (Ghidra, IDA, x64dbg) zisoma code.", "Ntuzigere ufungura dosiye ikekwa kuri telefone cyangwa mudasobwa yawe ngo «urebe icyo ikora». Yohereze kuri scanner yizewe, wibuke ko ibyo wohereje bishobora kugaragarira abandi, ntukohereze inyandiko z'ibanga."),
      ("Zana wachambuzi wanazotumia kusoma faili zinazotiliwa shaka kwa usalama: vichanganuzi na sandbox za mtandaoni (VirusTotal, Any.Run, Cuckoo) zinazoendesha faili na kuripoti tabia, na disassembler/debugger (Ghidra, IDA, x64dbg) zinazosoma msimbo.", "Kamwe usifungue faili inayotiliwa shaka kwenye kifaa chako «kuona inachofanya». Ipakie kwenye kichanganuzi cha kuaminika, ukikumbuka chochote unachopakia kinaweza kuonekana na wengine, hivyo usipakie nyaraka za faragha.")),
    T("forensic-tools", "Digital forensics tools (Autopsy, Volatility)", ["autopsy", "volatility", "ftk", "encase", "cellebrite", "forensic tools", "memory forensics", "disk forensics"], "operations", "forensic investigation", {"fr": "Outils d'investigation numérique", "sw": "Zana za uchunguzi wa kidijitali", "rw": "Ibikoresho by'iperereza rya digitale"},
      ("Software used to examine disks, memory and phones for evidence after an incident: Autopsy and FTK/EnCase (disk and file analysis), Volatility (memory analysis), Cellebrite (mobile devices).", "Investigators work on copies (forensic images), keep a chain of custody and document every step so evidence stays reliable. If you suspect a crime, do not keep using the device: preserve it and call the police or an incident team."),
      ("Logiciels pour examiner disques, mémoire et téléphones à la recherche de preuves après un incident : Autopsy et FTK/EnCase (analyse de disques et fichiers), Volatility (analyse de la mémoire), Cellebrite (appareils mobiles).", "Les enquêteurs travaillent sur des copies (images forensiques), tiennent une chaîne de traçabilité et documentent chaque étape pour que les preuves restent fiables. Si vous soupçonnez un crime, ne continuez pas d'utiliser l'appareil : préservez-le et appelez la police ou une équipe d'incident."),
      ("Porogaramu zikoreshwa mu gusuzuma disiki, memoire na telefone zishaka ibimenyetso nyuma y'igitero: Autopsy na FTK/EnCase (gusesengura disiki na dosiye), Volatility (gusesengura memoire), Cellebrite (telefone).", "Abashinzwe iperereza bakorera ku makopi (forensic images), bakagumana chain of custody kandi bakandika buri ntambwe kugira ngo ibimenyetso bikomeze kwizerwa. Ukeka icyaha, ntukomeze gukoresha igikoresho: kibike uhamagare polisi cyangwa itsinda ry'ibitero."),
      ("Programu zinazotumika kuchunguza diski, kumbukumbu na simu kutafuta ushahidi baada ya tukio: Autopsy na FTK/EnCase (uchambuzi wa diski na faili), Volatility (uchambuzi wa kumbukumbu), Cellebrite (vifaa vya simu).", "Wachunguzi hufanya kazi kwa nakala (forensic images), kuweka mnyororo wa umiliki na kuandika kila hatua ili ushahidi ubaki wa kuaminika. Ukishuku uhalifu, usiendelee kutumia kifaa: kihifadhi na upige simu polisi au timu ya matukio.")),
    T("log-sources-sysmon", "Security logs (Syslog, Sysmon, Windows Event Log)", ["syslog", "sysmon", "windows event log", "auditd", "event log", "security logs", "netflow", "zeek"], "operations", "log files", {"fr": "Journaux de sécurité (Syslog, Sysmon, journaux Windows)", "sw": "Kumbukumbu za usalama (Syslog, Sysmon, Windows Event Log)", "rw": "Logs z'umutekano (Syslog, Sysmon, Windows Event Log)"},
      ("The records that systems write about what happens on them: Syslog and auditd (Linux), Windows Event Log and Sysmon (Windows), NetFlow and Zeek (network). SIEM tools collect and correlate them.", "Good logging is how attacks are detected and investigated. Turn on logging for logins, admin actions and critical systems, send logs to a central protected place and keep them long enough to look back."),
      ("Les enregistrements que les systèmes écrivent sur ce qui s'y passe : Syslog et auditd (Linux), journaux d'événements Windows et Sysmon (Windows), NetFlow et Zeek (réseau). Les outils SIEM les collectent et les corrèlent.", "Une bonne journalisation permet de détecter et d'investiguer les attaques. Activez les journaux pour connexions, actions d'administration et systèmes critiques, envoyez-les vers un lieu central protégé et conservez-les assez longtemps."),
      ("Inyandiko sisitemu zandika ku byabaye kuri zo: Syslog na auditd (Linux), Windows Event Log na Sysmon (Windows), NetFlow na Zeek (umuyoboro). Ibikoresho bya SIEM birazikusanya bikazihuza.", "Logs nziza ni zo zituma ibitero bitahurwa bigakorerwa iperereza. Fungura logs z'uko binjira, ibikorwa bya admin na sisitemu z'ingenzi, uzohereze ahantu hamwe harinzwe kandi uzibike igihe gihagije."),
      ("Rekodi ambazo mifumo huandika kuhusu kinachotokea kwenye hiyo: Syslog na auditd (Linux), Windows Event Log na Sysmon (Windows), NetFlow na Zeek (mtandao). Zana za SIEM huzikusanya na kuzihusisha.", "Uwekaji kumbukumbu mzuri ndio njia ya kugundua na kuchunguza mashambulizi. Washa logi za kuingia, vitendo vya admin na mifumo muhimu, zituma mahali pamoja palipolindwa na uzihifadhi muda wa kutosha.")),
    T("threat-sharing-stix-misp", "Threat sharing (ISAC, STIX/TAXII, MISP)", ["isac", "stix", "taxii", "misp", "opencti", "threat sharing", "cyber threat sharing", "information sharing"], "operations", "network of organisations", {"fr": "Partage de menaces (ISAC, STIX/TAXII, MISP)", "sw": "Kushiriki vitisho (ISAC, STIX/TAXII, MISP)", "rw": "Gusangira amakuru y'ibitero (ISAC, STIX/TAXII, MISP)"},
      ("Ways defenders share information about attacks so others can protect themselves: ISACs (sector groups), STIX/TAXII (standard formats and transport) and platforms like MISP and OpenCTI.", "Sharing indicators (bad IP addresses, domains, file hashes) lets one victim's lesson protect many. National CERTs such as Rwanda's national cyber-security teams coordinate this; report incidents to them."),
      ("Moyens par lesquels les défenseurs partagent des informations sur les attaques pour que d'autres se protègent : ISAC (groupes sectoriels), STIX/TAXII (formats et transport standard) et plateformes comme MISP et OpenCTI.", "Partager des indicateurs (adresses IP, domaines, empreintes de fichiers malveillants) permet à la leçon d'une victime de protéger beaucoup d'autres. Les CERT nationaux, comme les équipes cybersécurité du Rwanda, coordonnent cela ; signalez-leur les incidents."),
      ("Uburyo abarinzi basangira amakuru ku bitero kugira ngo abandi bikingire: ISAC (amatsinda y'urwego), STIX/TAXII (imiterere n'ubwikorezi busanzwe) na platforms nka MISP na OpenCTI.", "Gusangira indicators (aderesi mbi za IP, domains, hash za dosiye) bituma isomo ry'uwahohotewe rirengera benshi. CERT z'igihugu, nk'amatsinda y'umutekano wa cyber y'u Rwanda, zibihuza; bimenyeshe ibitero."),
      ("Njia ambazo walinzi hushiriki taarifa kuhusu mashambulizi ili wengine wajilinde: ISAC (vikundi vya sekta), STIX/TAXII (miundo na usafirishaji wa kawaida) na majukwaa kama MISP na OpenCTI.", "Kushiriki viashiria (anwani mbaya za IP, vikoa, hash za faili) huwezesha funzo la mwathirika mmoja kulinda wengi. CERT za kitaifa, kama timu za usalama wa mtandao za Rwanda, huratibu hili; ziripotie matukio.")),
]
